  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The correct order is $2    < 1 < 3 < 4$. Since, more the number of $2^{\\circ}$ - NH- group, more is the basic nature.\r\n(1) Thus, 3 and 4 are more basic than 1 and 2 .\r\n(ii) Between 3 and 4,4 has one two - $\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group while 3 has only one $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group. $\\therefore 4$ is more basic than 3\r\n(iii) Between 1 and 2,1 has one $-\\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ group with no resonance, thus is more basic than 2.",
